            <p className="text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">Most hospital interview panels run on behavioral questions — they want evidence of how you acted, not how you&apos;d say you&apos;d act. The good news: every question on their list maps to one of five things they&apos;re grading (patient advocacy, safety speak-up, teamwork under stress, prioritization, integrity). Prepare 6-8 real shift stories and you can answer almost anything they ask.</p>
